      en: "HaBonim Fortress, also known as Qal'at al-Kharabsheh, is a 12th-century Crusader castle on the Mediterranean coast, about 30 km south of Haifa. Built around 1123 by the Crusaders, it was destroyed by the Mamluks under Baibars in 1265. The rectangular fortress features square towers at the corners, constructed from local sandstone. Excavations have revealed cisterns, stables, and living quarters. It served as a strategic point along the Via Maris, the ancient trade route between Egypt and Syria. Today it is a protected national park site.",
